            <title>[LU-21140] readdir of a directory that is splitting or migrating can return the same name twice</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21140</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;While a striped directory is being auto-split or migrated, a readdir on a client can return the same name twice, once from the old stripe and once from the new stripe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LMV reads each stripe in its own RPC and merges the pages by hash in lmv_striped_read_page() and lmv_dirent_next(). It never compares names. If a name is read from the old stripe before it moves and from the new stripe after it moves, it is listed twice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Impact&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A tool that processes the names in parallel fails on the second copy. For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;lfs find -type f -print0 DIR | xargs -0rP 16 -n 1 rm&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;fails with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;rm: cannot remove '...': No such file or directory&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No data is lost. The failure comes from deleting the same name twice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How to confirm&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Check the listing for duplicate names while the directory is migrating:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;lfs find --threads=4 -type f $TestDir | sort | uniq -d&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any output is a name that was listed more than once. The migrating flag in lfs getdirstripe $TestDir shows whether a migration is in progress.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
